export const SKILL_FILES: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
  "apple-watch-workouts/SKILL.md": "---\nname: apple-watch-workouts\ndescription: Turn a training idea into a custom workout on the Apple Watch with the dotworkout tools. Use when someone asks for an interval session, a swim set, a tempo run, FTP intervals, a HIIT circuit or any structured workout for their Watch, or wants to read one back.\nlicense: MIT\n---\n\n# Apple Watch workouts with dotworkout\n\nThe dotworkout tools build `.workout` files, the format the Workout app on the\nApple Watch uses for custom workouts. No model can write this format from\nmemory: it is undocumented binary, and what each sport accepts was read off a\nreal device. Let the tools do it.\n\n## The one rule: show the link\n\n`create_workout` returns a link. **The workout is inside the link**: it is\nencoded in the part after `#w=`, so nothing is stored anywhere and the link is\nthe only copy. Opening it on the iPhone shows the workout with a **Save the workout**\nbutton, and from there it goes to the Watch.\n\nSo every reply after `create_workout` must contain the full link, unchanged, on\nits own line. Do not shorten it, retype it, put \"[link]\" in its place, or leave\nit out because it is long. Do not try to rebuild the file from it either: one\ndropped character and the Watch refuses the workout.\n\nA good reply:\n\n> Here's your Norwegian 4×4: a 10 minute warm up, four 4 minute intervals in\n> zone 4 with 3 minute jogs, and a 5 minute cool down.\n>\n> Open this on your iPhone and tap Save the workout:\n>\n> https://workout.javierferrersb.dev/#w=…\n>\n> It opens in the Workout app from there. If it doesn't, save it to Files, open\n> it, tap Share and choose Workout.\n\n(Here the link is cut short with `…` only to keep this page readable. In a real\nreply paste the whole link `create_workout` gave you, however long.)\n\nA bad reply: \"Done! Your workout is ready, open the link above.\" — the user sees\nno link and the workout is gone.\n\nWhen running locally (Claude Code, desktop), `create_workout` also prints a QR\ncode and takes an optional `outputPath` to write the file to disk. Show the QR\nblock as it is, inside a code block so it keeps its shape, and still give the\nlink.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Check the sport.** Call `describe_activity` (one sport) or\n   `list_activities` (all of them). Support differs per sport and per location:\n   an indoor bike has no distance goal and no speed target, an indoor run has no\n   power or cadence, and only swimming has send-offs.\n2. **Write the plan as a spec** (format below). When the user gives zones,\n   paces or watts, use them; when they don't, pick sensible defaults and say\n   what you picked.\n3. **Validate** with `validate_workout`. It names the step that is wrong. Fix and\n   re-validate rather than guessing.\n4. **Create** with `create_workout` and give the user the link.\n5. To read a workout back (a link someone shared, or a file), use\n   `inspect_workout`.\n\n## The spec\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"location\": \"outdoor\",\n  \"name\": \"Norwegian 4×4\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"10min\", \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 2 } },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 4,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"4:00\" },\n      \"rest\": \"3:00\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 4 }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"5min\" }\n}\n```\n\n- `activity`: one of the names `list_activities` returns, such as `RUNNING`,\n  `CYCLING`, `SWIMMING`, `HIGH_INTENSITY_INTERVAL_TRAINING`, `ROWING`.\n- `location`: `outdoor` or `indoor`, for sports offered both ways. It changes\n  what is allowed. Pool swims are `outdoor` (Apple stores them that way).\n- `blocks`: the main set, in order. Each block is `repeat` × `work`, with an\n  optional `rest` after each repetition, an optional `alert` (target) on the\n  work, and an optional `label`. A one-off step is a block with `repeat: 1`.\n- `warmup` / `cooldown`: optional single steps that take the same `alert` and\n  `label`.\n\n### Goals: every step has one\n\n| Goal     | Write                   | Notes                                     |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Time     | `{ \"time\": \"4:00\" }`    | `\"4:00\"`, `\"90s\"`, `\"10min\"`, `\"1:15:00\"` |\n| Distance | `{ \"distance\": \"5km\" }` | `\"400m\"`, `\"5km\"`, `\"1mi\"`, `\"200yd\"`     |\n| Open     | `{ \"open\": true }`      | No goal; the wearer ends the step         |\n| Send-off | distance + `sendOff`    | Swimming only: `\"sendOff\": \"1:45\"`        |\n\nTwo traps:\n\n- **A bare number is seconds or the sport's default unit.** `\"10\"` as a time is\n  10 seconds; write `\"10min\"` or `\"10:00\"`. `\"400\"` as a running distance is\n  400 **km**, because running, cycling, walking and hiking default to km;\n  swimming and rowing default to metres. Always write the unit.\n- `\"1:00\"` is one minute and `\"1:00:00\"` is one hour.\n\n### Targets (`alert`)\n\n| Kind             | Example                                                       |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `heartRateZone`  | `{ \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 4 }`                      |\n| `heartRateRange` | `{ \"kind\": \"heartRateRange\", \"from\": 140, \"to\": 155 }`        |\n| `pace`           | `{ \"kind\": \"pace\", \"pace\": \"4:30/km\" }`                       |\n| `paceRange`      | `{ \"kind\": \"paceRange\", \"from\": \"4:40/km\", \"to\": \"4:25/km\" }` |\n| `kmh`            | `{ \"kind\": \"kmh\", \"kmh\": 32 }`                                |\n| `kmhRange`       | `{ \"kind\": \"kmhRange\", \"from\": 28, \"to\": 32 }`                |\n| `power`          | `{ \"kind\": \"power\", \"watts\": 250 }`                           |\n| `powerRange`     | `{ \"kind\": \"powerRange\", \"from\": 240, \"to\": 255 }`            |\n| `cadence`        | `{ \"kind\": \"cadence\", \"perMinute\": 90 }`                      |\n| `cadenceRange`   | `{ \"kind\": \"cadenceRange\", \"from\": 85, \"to\": 95 }`            |\n\nPaces work in `/km` and `/mi`; the server converts them. Heart-rate zones are\nthe wearer's own zones on the Watch, so a zone is usually better than made-up\nbeats per minute.\n\nWhat each sport takes (`list_activities` is the authority if this ever differs):\n\n| Sport                                                          | Goals                          | Targets                           |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------------------------- |\n| Running, outdoor                                               | distance, time, open           | heart rate, pace, cadence, power  |\n| Running, indoor                                                | distance, time, open           | heart rate, pace                  |\n| Cycling, outdoor                                               | distance, time, open           | heart rate, speed, cadence, power |\n| Cycling, indoor                                                | time, open                     | heart rate, cadence, power        |\n| Swimming                                                       | distance, send-off, time, open | heart rate                        |\n| Rowing, outdoor                                                | distance, time, open           | heart rate                        |\n| Rowing, indoor                                                 | time, open                     | heart rate                        |\n| Walking, hiking                                                | distance, time, open           | heart rate                        |\n| HIIT, strength, core, yoga, elliptical, stairs, cross training | time, open                     | heart rate                        |\n\n### Labels\n\n`label` is free text shown on the Watch during the step. Swimming has no stroke\nfield, so the stroke goes here: `\"label\": \"free\"`, `\"kick\"`, `\"IM\"`. For\nstrength work it names the exercise: `\"label\": \"burpees\"`.\n\n## Examples\n\n`references/examples.md` has a library of real workouts, each with the request,\nthe exact `create_workout` arguments and how to reply: Norwegian 4×4 (run and\nbike), swim pyramid, send-off sets, IM, tempo runs, track 400s, mile repeats,\nlong runs, FTP 2×20, 30/30s, cadence drills, Tabata, rowing, walking and\nstrength circuits. There is also a list of mistakes the validator catches.\nEvery example there is checked by the dotworkout test suite.\n",
  "apple-watch-workouts/references/examples.md": "# Worked examples\n\nEach one is a request someone might make, the exact arguments to pass to\n`create_workout` (the same object works for `validate_workout`), and notes on\nthe choices. Every `json` block on this page is built and validated by the\ndotworkout test suite, so these are known to produce files the Watch accepts.\n\nAfter `create_workout`, always reply with the full link it returns, on its own\nline. See \"The one rule\" in SKILL.md.\n\n## Running\n\n### Norwegian 4×4\n\n> \"Build me a Norwegian 4×4 for tomorrow's run.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"name\": \"Norwegian 4×4\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"10min\", \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 2 } },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 4,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"4:00\" },\n      \"rest\": \"3:00\",\n      \"label\": \"hard\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 4 }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"5min\", \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 1 } }\n}\n```\n\nThe protocol is four 4 minute efforts at 85–95% of max heart rate with 3 minute\nactive recoveries. Zone 4 is the closest Watch zone. The recovery after the last\ninterval is part of the set, so the cool down can be short.\n\n### Tempo run on a pace band\n\n> \"Tempo run: 2 km easy, 5 km at 4:30 to 4:40 per km, 1 km easy.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"name\": \"Tempo 5K\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"2km\", \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 2 } },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 1,\n      \"work\": { \"distance\": \"5km\" },\n      \"label\": \"tempo\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"paceRange\", \"from\": \"4:40/km\", \"to\": \"4:30/km\" }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"1km\" }\n}\n```\n\nPaces go in as written; the server converts them. The order of `from` and `to`\ndoes not matter.\n\n### Track 400s\n\n> \"8 × 400 m at 5K pace (3:50/km) with 90 seconds standing rest.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"name\": \"8 × 400\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"2km\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 8,\n      \"work\": { \"distance\": \"400m\" },\n      \"rest\": \"1:30\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"pace\", \"pace\": \"3:50/km\" }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"1km\" }\n}\n```\n\n`\"400m\"`, never `\"400\"`: running defaults to kilometres.\n\n### Mile repeats, in miles\n\n> \"Four mile repeats at 7:00 pace, two minutes jog between.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"name\": \"Mile repeats\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"1mi\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 4,\n      \"work\": { \"distance\": \"1mi\" },\n      \"rest\": \"2:00\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"pace\", \"pace\": \"7:00/mi\" }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"1mi\" }\n}\n```\n\nUnits are kept as written, so the Watch shows miles.\n\n### Easy long run\n\n> \"90 minute long run, keep me in zone 2.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"name\": \"Long run\",\n  \"blocks\": [\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"1:30:00\" }, \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 2 } }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nA single steady effort is one block with `repeat: 1`. `\"1:30:00\"` is 90\nminutes; `\"1:30\"` would be 90 seconds.\n\n### Treadmill progression\n\n> \"Treadmill run, 3 × 8 minutes getting faster: 5:30, 5:10, 4:50 per km.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"location\": \"indoor\",\n  \"name\": \"Treadmill progression\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"10min\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"8min\" }, \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"pace\", \"pace\": \"5:30/km\" } },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"8min\" }, \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"pace\", \"pace\": \"5:10/km\" } },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"8min\" }, \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"pace\", \"pace\": \"4:50/km\" } }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"5min\" }\n}\n```\n\nIndoors a run takes pace and heart rate only: no cadence, no power.\n\n## Cycling\n\n### FTP 2 × 20 on the trainer\n\n> \"2 × 20 at threshold on the turbo. My FTP is 265.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"CYCLING\",\n  \"location\": \"indoor\",\n  \"name\": \"2 × 20 threshold\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"15min\", \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"powerRange\", \"from\": 130, \"to\": 180 } },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 2,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"20min\" },\n      \"rest\": \"5min\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"powerRange\", \"from\": 240, \"to\": 255 }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"10min\" }\n}\n```\n\n240–255 W is 91–96% of 265. Work out the watts from the FTP the user gives; say\nwhat range you chose. Indoor cycling has no distance goal and no speed target.\n\n### Norwegian 4×4 on the bike\n\n> \"Same 4×4 but on the indoor bike.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"CYCLING\",\n  \"location\": \"indoor\",\n  \"name\": \"Norwegian 4×4 bike\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"10min\", \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 2 } },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 4,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"4:00\" },\n      \"rest\": \"3:00\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 4 }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"5min\" }\n}\n```\n\n### 30/30 VO2 max\n\n> \"Ten 30/30s at 400 watts.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"CYCLING\",\n  \"location\": \"indoor\",\n  \"name\": \"30/30s\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"15min\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 10,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"30s\" },\n      \"rest\": \"30s\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"power\", \"watts\": 400 }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"10min\" }\n}\n```\n\n### Outdoor cadence and speed\n\n> \"Road ride: 5 × 1 minute high cadence, 100 to 110, then 20 km steady at about 30 km/h.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"CYCLING\",\n  \"name\": \"Spin-ups and steady\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"10min\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 5,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"1:00\" },\n      \"rest\": \"1:00\",\n      \"label\": \"spin\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"cadenceRange\", \"from\": 100, \"to\": 110 }\n    },\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 1,\n      \"work\": { \"distance\": \"20km\" },\n      \"label\": \"steady\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"kmhRange\", \"from\": 28, \"to\": 32 }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"10min\" }\n}\n```\n\nSpeed targets are outdoor only.\n\n## Swimming\n\n### Pyramid\n\n> \"A swimming pyramid, 50 up to 200 and back, 20 seconds rest.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"SWIMMING\",\n  \"name\": \"Pyramid\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"400\", \"label\": \"easy free\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"50\" }, \"rest\": \":20\", \"label\": \"free\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"100\" }, \"rest\": \":20\", \"label\": \"free\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"150\" }, \"rest\": \":20\", \"label\": \"free\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"200\" }, \"rest\": \":20\", \"label\": \"free\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"150\" }, \"rest\": \":20\", \"label\": \"free\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"100\" }, \"rest\": \":20\", \"label\": \"free\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"50\" }, \"rest\": \":20\", \"label\": \"free\" }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"200\", \"label\": \"easy\" }\n}\n```\n\nSwimming defaults to metres, so a bare `\"400\"` is 400 m. Laps are not in the\nfile: pool length is chosen on the Watch when the swim starts.\n\n### Send-off set\n\n> \"10 × 100 free on 1:45.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"SWIMMING\",\n  \"name\": \"10 × 100 on 1:45\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"300\" },\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 10, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"100\" }, \"sendOff\": \"1:45\", \"label\": \"free\" }],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"200\" }\n}\n```\n\nA send-off means \"leave every 1:45 however fast you finish\", so there is no\n`rest`. Only swimming has send-offs.\n\n### Individual medley\n\n> \"IM set: 4 × 25 of each stroke, then 4 × 100 IM, 15 seconds rest.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"SWIMMING\",\n  \"name\": \"IM set\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"400\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    { \"repeat\": 4, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"25\" }, \"rest\": \":15\", \"label\": \"fly\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 4, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"25\" }, \"rest\": \":15\", \"label\": \"back\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 4, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"25\" }, \"rest\": \":15\", \"label\": \"breast\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 4, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"25\" }, \"rest\": \":15\", \"label\": \"free\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 4, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"100\" }, \"rest\": \":15\", \"label\": \"IM\" }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"200\" }\n}\n```\n\nThere is no stroke field; the label carries it and the Watch shows it during\nthe step.\n\n### Yards\n\n> \"Masters set in a yards pool: 6 × 200 yd on 3:00.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"SWIMMING\",\n  \"name\": \"6 × 200 yd\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"500yd\" },\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 6, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"200yd\" }, \"sendOff\": \"3:00\" }],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"200yd\" }\n}\n```\n\n## Everything else\n\n### Tabata\n\n> \"A Tabata: 8 rounds of 20 seconds all out, 10 seconds off.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"HIGH_INTENSITY_INTERVAL_TRAINING\",\n  \"name\": \"Tabata\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"5min\" },\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 8, \"work\": { \"time\": \"20s\" }, \"rest\": \"10s\", \"label\": \"all out\" }],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"5min\" }\n}\n```\n\n### Strength circuit\n\n> \"Five rounds: 45 seconds each of squats, push-ups and burpees, 15 seconds between, a minute between rounds.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"FUNCTIONAL_STRENGTH_TRAINING\",\n  \"name\": \"Full-body circuit\",\n  \"blocks\": [\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"squats\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"push-ups\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"1:00\", \"label\": \"burpees\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"squats\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"push-ups\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"1:00\", \"label\": \"burpees\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"squats\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"push-ups\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"1:00\", \"label\": \"burpees\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"squats\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"push-ups\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"1:00\", \"label\": \"burpees\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"squats\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"rest\": \"15s\", \"label\": \"push-ups\" },\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"45s\" }, \"label\": \"burpees\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nA `repeat` covers one step and its rest, so a circuit of different exercises is\nwritten out round by round. Strength sports take time and open goals only.\n\n### Sets you finish yourself\n\n> \"Three sets of max push-ups, two minutes between.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"TRADITIONAL_STRENGTH_TRAINING\",\n  \"name\": \"Max push-ups\",\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 3, \"work\": { \"open\": true }, \"rest\": \"2:00\", \"label\": \"max push-ups\" }]\n}\n```\n\nAn open step has no goal; the wearer taps to end it.\n\n### Indoor rowing\n\n> \"Erg session: 4 × 8 minutes in zone 3, 2 minutes easy between.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"ROWING\",\n  \"location\": \"indoor\",\n  \"name\": \"4 × 8 erg\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"time\": \"10min\" },\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 4,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"8min\" },\n      \"rest\": \"2:00\",\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateZone\", \"zone\": 3 }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"time\": \"5min\" }\n}\n```\n\nIndoor rowing has no distance goal. Outdoors it does:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"ROWING\",\n  \"name\": \"3 × 2000 m\",\n  \"warmup\": { \"distance\": \"1000\" },\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 3, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"2000\" }, \"rest\": \"4:00\" }],\n  \"cooldown\": { \"distance\": \"1000\" }\n}\n```\n\n### Brisk walk\n\n> \"30 minute brisk walk, heart rate 110 to 125.\"\n\n```json\n{\n  \"activity\": \"WALKING\",\n  \"name\": \"Brisk walk\",\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"repeat\": 1,\n      \"work\": { \"time\": \"30min\" },\n      \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"heartRateRange\", \"from\": 110, \"to\": 125 }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Mistakes the validator catches\n\nEach of these fails `validate_workout` with an error naming the step. They are\nhere so you know what not to write; the test suite checks that each one fails.\n\nA power target on a swim: swimming takes heart rate only.\n\n```json invalid\n{\n  \"activity\": \"SWIMMING\",\n  \"blocks\": [\n    { \"repeat\": 4, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"100\" }, \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"power\", \"watts\": 200 } }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nA distance on an indoor bike: the trainer measures no distance.\n\n```json invalid\n{\n  \"activity\": \"CYCLING\",\n  \"location\": \"indoor\",\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"20km\" } }]\n}\n```\n\nA send-off on a run: only swimming has them. Use `rest` instead.\n\n```json invalid\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 6, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"400m\" }, \"sendOff\": \"2:00\" }]\n}\n```\n\nA pace target on a treadmill is fine, but cadence is not:\n\n```json invalid\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"location\": \"indoor\",\n  \"blocks\": [\n    { \"repeat\": 1, \"work\": { \"time\": \"20min\" }, \"alert\": { \"kind\": \"cadence\", \"perMinute\": 180 } }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nA bare distance on a run: `\"400\"` is 400 km, so the server warns. Write\n`\"400m\"`.\n\n```json warning\n{\n  \"activity\": \"RUNNING\",\n  \"blocks\": [{ \"repeat\": 8, \"work\": { \"distance\": \"400\" }, \"rest\": \"1:30\" }]\n}\n```\n",
};
